I just came across a PCI sparc MB here which I'd like to get running.

I'm told it was purchased about on year ago and that they gave up on
it because they couldn't find a video card it liked.  (Something about
requiring an exact version of a given Mach64 card or some such.)

- From Sun's website I see that it is a AXi rev 05 MB.  There are two
64M RAM sticks (though I don't know whether they are 11 bit or 10 bit;
in any case the slots they were in were not a pair as specified in the
OEM docs...).  There was a 4M ATI 3D RAGE II+ Mach64 card on hand, but
I am not getting any responce from it; the monitor indicates that
there is no signal at all from the card.

[time passws...]

[SIGH] Now it won't even power up, though a 5.0V potential does
remain between the pins of jumper 3301 (the front, momentary-contact
powere switch).

So, does anyone have any tips?  Does it matter which PCI slot the vga
card is in?  Does just any Mach64 card work?

